<title>UK: London Tea Auction price indications.</title>
<headline>London Tea Auction price indications.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>At today's London landed Tea Auction of 3,819 packages of 53.50 kgs, including 1,400 offshore, price indications in pence a kilo compared to the last sale and the corresponding week last year.</p>
<p>    Best available  175   (171 and 179)</p>
<p>    Good		125   (125 and 135)</p>
<p>    Good Medium     117   (117 and 120)</p>
<p>    Medium	    109   (107 and 100)</p>
<p>    Low Medium	 90   ( 90 and  88)</p>
<p>The highest price paid was 175 pence for a Ceylon BOPF.</p>
</text>
